    "value": "The resident had a long-standing issue with infestations of rats in the property that had been ongoing for over 4 years. On 28 November 2023, the resident raised a complaint saying she had an infestation of rats in her loft and walls. The landlord had previously confirmed the rats were coming from her next-door neighbour's garden and had replaced the roof, but the rats were still able to get into her property. She had used baiting traps in the garden, but they did not work. The landlord issued its stage 1 response on 1 December 2023, saying it would contact the resident and arrange for a contractor to inspect the property and carry out pest treatments. On 8 March 2024, the resident asked to escalate her complaint to stage 2, saying rats continued to enter her loft and the landlord had failed to take any action. On 8 July 2024, the resident again requested to escalate her complaint to stage 2, saying rats continued to enter her garden despite a new wooden fence, a roofing company found an entry point in the loft but the landlord did not fix it, and the property smelled of rat urine. The landlord issued its stage 2 response on 5 August 2024, apologising for the ongoing rat issues and acknowledging it had been difficult to find the source of the infestation. It said it would arrange a joint visit with its Housing Officer and Repairs Team Leader to inspect the property and agree an action plan. The resident asked this Service to investigate because the issue had been ongoing for over 4 years and the landlord had still not resolved it, impacting her mental health and use of her home.",
